⚠️ Pin rationale: 3.1.5 is the newest tag on the maintained 3.1.x line as of
   vendoring date. The library's `main` branch has since moved to a 4.x
   pre-release (4.0.0-beta1) that depends on phpseclib/phpseclib -- NOT
   vendorable under this project's "no Composer / few plain PHP files"
   Dreamhost-shared-hosting constraint -- so 3.1.x (openssl-only) is the
   deliberate, permanent-for-now choice, not a temporary lag.

Files vendored under src/ (4 files, ~2,540 lines total):
  XMLSecurityKey.php   -- key material + sign()/verify()/encryptData()/decryptData()
  XMLSecurityDSig.php  -- XML-DSig: SignedInfo/Reference/Signature construction,
                          canonicalization, locateSignature()/verify() for inbound
  XMLSecEnc.php        -- XML-Enc (NOT used in v1 -- SIGNula refuses SPs that set
                          wantAssertionsEncrypted; vendored because it is part of
                          the single upstream release and SamlXmlLibLoader loads
                          the release as one unit, not because it is called)
  Utils/XPath.php      -- small internal XPath-registration helper the two
                          classes above both depend on

⚠️ SECURITY MAINTENANCE: this is security-critical XML-signature crypto --
   the exact class of library responsible for the 2012-2018 XML Signature
   Wrapping (XSW) vulnerability wave across SAML implementations (Somorovsky
   et al., "On Breaking SAML: Be Whoever You Want to Be"; CVE-2019-3465 was a
   real xmlseclibs advisory, fixed at 3.0.4+). Track upstream advisories at
   https://github.com/robrichards/xmlseclibs/security/advisories and the
   GHSA feed, and bump this vendored copy when a fixed release ships. Record
   the new version here and in _docs/setup/SECURITY_SETUP.md.

   Per the SAML IdP dormant-foundation plan (issue #100), ALL calls into this
   library are made through EXACTLY ONE project-owned facade --
   web/private_html/security/SamlXmlSignature.php -- which pins a
   single-algorithm allowlist (exclusive C14N, RSA-SHA256, SHA-256 digest,
   enveloped-signature transform) and exposes ONLY signAssertion() /
   signResponse() / verifyEnvelopedSignature(). Nothing else in SIGNula
   references `RobRichards\XMLSecLibs\*` directly. Verification of
   attacker-supplied XML (C3, POST-binding signed requests) additionally
   requires a dedicated XSW-hardening red-team pass (see PRE_LAUNCH_REVIEW.md)
   before `wantAuthnRequestsSigned=1` is ever honoured over the POST binding
   -- this is independent of the library itself being sound.

How it is loaded (no Composer autoload in prod):
  web/private_html/security/SamlXmlLibLoader.php require_once's these files
  explicitly (with file_exists() guards) in dependency order -- mirrors
  web/private_html/security/JwtLibLoader.php for firebase/php-jwt. The
  project-owned facade web/private_html/security/SamlXmlSignature.php is the
  ONLY class the rest of the codebase calls.
